{"schema_version":"1.0.0","id":"cik-0001786352","cik":"0001786352","slug":"bill-holdings-786352","name":"BILL Holdings, Inc.","ticker":"BILL","exchanges":["NYSE"],"sector":"Services-Prepackaged Software","sic":"7372","country":"CA","website":"","listed_years":5.9,"first_annual":"2020-08-31","last_filing":"2026-06-17","annual_only":false,"edgar_url":"https://www.sec.gov/cgi-bin/browse-edgar?action=getcompany&CIK=0001786352&type=10-K","summary":{"sentences":["BILL Holdings, Inc. files with the SEC under \"Services-Prepackaged Software\", based in CA, and has been publicly reporting for 6 years.","It reported $1.6bn of revenue over the trailing four quarters, up 13.5% against the same quarter a year earlier, at a gross margin of 81.6%.","Listed on NYSE, it funds itself from operations ($257.2m of operating cash flow over the year)."],"generated":true,"note":"Assembled from filing metadata and XBRL figures. Not editorial judgement - and rule 7 asks whether *you* can explain it, so rewrite this in your own words before you rely on it."},"bull":[{"text":"Revenue grew 13.5% year on year (Q1 2026 vs Q1 2025), reaching $406.6m in the quarter.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1786352/000162828026032387/0001628280-26-032387-index.htm","accession":"0001628280-26-032387"},{"text":"Growth has been positive in all 8 year-on-year comparisons, so this is a trend rather than one good quarter.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1786352/000162828026032387/0001628280-26-032387-index.htm","accession":"0001628280-26-032387"},{"text":"Gross margin of 81.6% means most of each additional sale falls through to cover fixed costs.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1786352/000162828026032387/0001628280-26-032387-index.htm","accession":"0001628280-26-032387"},{"text":"Operating cash flow is positive at $257.2m over the trailing year, so the business funds itself and is not dependent on raising money.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1786352/000162828025050328/0001628280-25-050328-index.htm","accession":"0001628280-25-050328"}],"bear":[{"text":"The company is loss-making at the operating line (-0.1% margin). Profitability is a forecast, not a fact.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1786352/000162828026032387/0001628280-26-032387-index.htm","accession":"0001628280-26-032387"},{"text":"Diluted share count rose 10.2% over the year (Q1 2026 vs Q1 2025). The company can grow while your share of it shrinks, and this is the number most commentary ignores.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1786352/000162828026032387/0001628280-26-032387-index.htm","accession":"0001628280-26-032387"},{"text":"Insiders disposed of 8.9% of their combined holdings over the last four quarters (32,875 shares across 14 ownership filings). People with the best view of the business were reducing their stake.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1786352/000206742526000001/0002067425-26-000001-index.htm"},{"text":"Officers and directors hold only 0.3% of the shares. There is little alignment between what happens to the share price and what happens to them.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1786352/000206742526000001/0002067425-26-000001-index.htm"},{"text":"Base rate: 57.8% of US common stocks underperformed one-month Treasury bills over their lifetimes (Bessembinder, Journal of Financial Economics, 2018). Nothing above changes that starting point.","source_url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jfineco.2018.06.004"}],"triggers":[{"id":"gross_margin_floor","kind":"metric","label":"Gross margin falls below 74.0% for 2 consecutive quarters","metric":"gross_margin","comparison":"below","threshold":0.74,"consecutive":2,"current":0.816,"current_display":"81.6%","threshold_display":"74.0%","fired":false,"rationale":"Eight points of margin is a real deterioration rather than noise. Two consecutive quarters stops one bad quarter from forcing a s